<title>GREECE: Bank of Greece 96 profit 36.6bln drachmas.</title>
<headline>Bank of Greece 96 profit 36.6bln drachmas.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Greece posted pretax profits of 36.6 billion drachmas, up 5.0 percent from 34.85 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Its board will propose a dividend per share of 1,300 drachmas for fiscal 1996 from 1,200 drachmas in 1995, it said.</p>
<p>The Bank of Greece is the country's central bank and one of the few EU central banks listed on an exchange.</p>
<p>Gross revenues from interest, commissions and other profits from banking services in Greece and abroad rose to 92 billion in 1996 from 85 billion in 1995, it said.</p>
